    {
      "number": 1,
      "id": "PR_kwDOKyxaFM6dRCvw",
      "title": "Add v1 and v2 exception",
      "url": "https://github.com/CBonnell/lamps-keyusage-crl-validation-clarification/pull/1",
      "state": "MERGED",
      "author": "CBonnell",
      "authorAssociation": "OWNER",
      "assignees": [],
      "labels": [],
      "body": "MSJ pointed out that v1 trust anchors are still encountered. Add a carve-out for this legacy use of v1 (and v2, if any such certificates exist in the wild).",
      "createdAt": "2025-07-03T13:04:07Z",
      "updatedAt": "2025-07-07T18:50:46Z",
      "baseRepository": "CBonnell/lamps-keyusage-crl-validation-clarification",
      "baseRefName": "main",
      "baseRefOid": "cccdd4e818754fb82f34359a0c2934cc2578bc9c",
      "headRepository": "CBonnell/lamps-keyusage-crl-validation-clarification",
      "headRefName": "v1-v2-exception",
      "headRefOid": "a0078fbc699c112ccee896682f53a7f6719d8084",
      "closedAt": "2025-07-07T18:50:40Z",
      "mergedAt": "2025-07-07T18:50:40Z",
      "mergedBy": "CBonnell",
      "mergeCommit": {
        "oid": "b8f85c5ff05af37b46f1634481fa81b54213d9f5"
      },
      "comments": [],
      "reviews": [
        {
          "id": "PRR_kwDOKyxaFM6yVmc8",
          "commit": {
            "abbreviatedOid": "a0078fb"
          },
          "author": "tadahik",
          "authorAssociation": "COLLABORATOR",
          "state": "COMMENTED",
          "body": "It looks good to me.\r\n\r\nIf an implementation is only used for v3 certificate,\r\nthat implementation might not need to check if version is 3 or not, according to later sentence of following text.\r\n\r\n(from RFC 5280 Section 6.3)\r\n> Conforming implementations that support CRLs\r\n> are not required to implement this algorithm, but they MUST be\r\n> functionally equivalent to the external behavior resulting from this\r\n> procedure when processing CRLs that are issued in conformance with\r\n> this profile.  Any algorithm may be used by a particular\r\n> implementation so long as it derives the correct result.",
          "createdAt": "2025-07-07T02:44:07Z",
          "updatedAt": "2025-07-07T04:14:58Z",
          "comments": []
        }
      ]
    },
